        "filename": "McLean County Courthouse and Square (7436726814).jpg",
        "caption": "The McLean County Courthouse &amp; Square in Bloomington (1903). It was the home of the McLean County Circuit Court from 1900 to 1976. A fire damaged the building three years later, and it was redesigned by three of Bloomington's most notable architects: George Miller, Arthur Pillsbury, and Paul Moratz. In the 1980s, the McLean County Historical Society opened a museum in the former courthouse.",
